Who We Are:
NTT DATA is part of NTT Group, one of the largest ICT providers in the world with revenues of over USD 100B and over 193,000 employees worldwide. NTT DATA is a world-leading System Integration and Consulting company, with a Card & Payments Division of over 1,000 employees, and payment systems processing over 460 million transactions per month. NTT Data has established its global payment hub headquarters in Hong Kong, which is responsible for spearheading and expanding the payment service provider and acquiring services worldwide to our premium client base which represents over 10,000 enterprise class clients and 80% of the Fortune Global 100.
Who We Are Looking For:
We are currently seeking a highly competent and experienced Business Analyst / Solution Analyst to join NTT DATA’s global payment hub, which is headquartered in Hong Kong. As a Business Analyst / Solution Analyst, you will turn business requirements into well-designed application solutions. By analyzing needs, exploring technology options, and producing clear functional design documents, you will bridge business and technical teams—ensuring smooth development and high-quality delivery.
>Job Responsibilities
Analyze business needs and define operational objectives by gathering and validating requirements, including output formats and expected results
Design end-to-end solutions, including workflows, system architecture, network diagrams, and logic flows based on system capabilities
Develop clear and detailed functional specifications, including requirements documents, RESTful API specifications, and acceptance criteria
Oversee system integration, testing (QA), and deployment to ensure smooth and quality delivery
Continuously enhance system performance by reviewing current practices and recommending improvements
Ensure solutions are sustainable and compliant with relevant regulations (e.g., data governance, security standards such as PCI-DSS)
Monitor project progress, resolve issues, and provide regular status updates with actionable recommendations
Strengthen processes and controls by identifying gaps and proposing improvements
Maintain strong stakeholder engagement through proactive and effective communication
Prepare analytical and technical reports to support decision-making and identify trends
Support team collaboration and contribute to overall team success
Provide data-driven recommendations to senior management and actively support implementation of approved changes
Job Requirements
Bachelor’s Degree in appropriate field of study;
1 – 2 years of relevant experience;
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate complex business needs into practical solutions;
Technical aptitude and willingness to learn technologies such as Java, JavaScript, MySQL, and cloud platforms;
Experience in process analysis, solution design, and documentation within enterprise-level projects;
Familiarity with UI/UX concepts, including application flows and basic mockup design;
Excellent communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills;
Detail-oriented, well-organized, and able to manage multiple tasks effectively;
Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment;
Proactive mindset with strong critical thinking skills;
Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese, and
Prior exposure to the payments industry or regulated environments is an advantage.
>

