The Independent Schools Foundation Academy (The ISF Academy) has a deep commitment to Hong Kong, inspiring Pre-Primary to Grade 12 learners to act as empowered global stewards since its establishment in 2003. As an internationally accredited private independent school, our unique student-focused academic curriculum and experiential learning programs are deeply rooted in Chinese culture combined with a truly bi-lingual and intercultural learning environment. ISF’s exceptional IB Diploma Programme performance over many cohorts, has seen graduates accepted at the world’s most prestigious universities to continue their next stage of learning. The school currently has around 2600 students and 530 employees across the ISF Pre-School and Academy.
We are now seeking a self-driven, passionate and experienced candidate to fill the following position:
Education Technology Systems Analyst (Ref: ETC/ETSA/20260526/jdb)
Job Responsibilities:
Manage, develop, and maintain education technology systems and applications, including the School’s LMS (e.g., Moodle);
Perform system configuration, updates, troubleshooting, and annual rollover tasks to ensure stable and effective operations;
Integrate education technology platforms with internal and external systems through APIs and other integration methods;
Participate in the full application development lifecycle, including design, development, testing, deployment, and enhancement;
Work closely with the Head of Education Technology, Head of IT, and Academic staff to design and deliver systems that support teaching, learning, and student digital portfolios;
Collaborate with divisional stakeholders to assess platform usage, identify needs, and recommend improvements;
Provide in-person and written support to teachers, students, colleagues and parents on the use of education technology platforms and related services;
Create and maintain clear technical documentation, user guides, and training materials.
Maintain system updates, debugging processes, data sharing, and platform performance monitoring;
Support the uploading, embedding, and management of multimedia content across education technology systems;
Promote effective and consistent use of education technology platforms in alignment with the School’s mission, vision, and educational technology strategy; and
Support continuous improvement initiatives to enhance digital learning experiences.
Requirements:
Bachelor's Degree holder or above, preferably in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field;
At least 5 years of relevant development or systems experience;
Solid hands-on experience in web application development and support, including PHP, HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, SQL, jQuery, and Ajax;
Experience working with web APIs and integrating (linking) different internal and external platforms or systems;
Practical experience with version control systems, preferably Git, and familiarity with collaborative development environments;
An advantage to have experience working with or developing LMS (e.g. Moodle or other LMS platforms), including experience in LAMP-based environments (Linux, Apache, MySQL, PHP) and web services or integrations such as SOAP, REST, or XML;
Well-organized, detail-oriented, and able to handle confidential information appropriately;
Good interpersonal and communication skills;
A self-starter and self-motivated autonomous worker with effective time management abilities;
Good command of written and spoken English; proficiency in Chinese (Cantonese & and Putonghua) is an advantage.
The ISF Foundation, Academy & Pre-School are committed to ensuring safety and well-being of our students. We hold high standards of recruitment practices with specific attention to child protection. All applicants must be willing to undergo relevant background checks and screenings.
